# Dagric OS Pro — Virtual machines ("Windows in a window")
# Wine/Bottles cover most Windows apps; for the rest, the honest answer is
# real Windows in a VM. Fully open-source stack: KVM (kernel hypervisor),
# QEMU, libvirt, and the virt-manager GUI. Windows itself is NEVER bundled —
# the dagric-vm helper points at Microsoft's official ISO download.
# Enabled on demand via dagric-vm (group membership needs owner consent).

# The GUI the owner actually opens
virt-manager

# Hypervisor + tooling
qemu-system-x86
qemu-utils
libvirt-daemon-system
libvirt-clients

# UEFI firmware for guests — Windows 11 requires UEFI boot
ovmf

# Software TPM 2.0 — Windows 11's hardware requirement, satisfied in software
swtpm
swtpm-tools

# Guest display/console viewer (SPICE)
virt-viewer

# NAT networking for guests (libvirt's default network)
dnsmasq-base
